So `vterm-clear` sends `Ctrl-L` to the terminal, which is the standard "clear screen" command. The issue is that `vterm-clear` likely leaves some control characters in the buffer. Let me examine the actual buffer content more carefully.

Let me also search for information about the `^L` character - this is the form feed character (ASCII 12).

